From 72ed0e5bbe332db3aba763293e4248d2da6474ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:22:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 105/270] ARM: bring up the other CPUs (SMP), started through
 PSCI

Loader: the CPUs whose enable-method is PSCI are started on a second entry
point of the trampoline page. With their MMU and caches off they invalidate
their L1 data cache, report they are up and wait until the kernel arguments
are in place, then take the common path into the kernel with their CPU
number. Only the CPUs that came up are counted. All Normal and Device memory
is now Shareable (PRRR NS0/DS0) and the table walks too, so that the caches
of the CPUs are coherent; TTBCR was set from a register that is now the CPU
number.

Kernel: per CPU exception mode stacks, exception setup and topology,
inter-processor interrupts through the interrupt controller, and the banked
parts of the GIC and of the generic timer set up on each CPU.

In QEMU (virt, 2 Cortex-A15) a computation runs 1.84 times faster on two
threads. The Tegra 2 start sequence and timer come next.
